Chapter: IdentityCapGate

 The parent labels itself, spawns a child, and strips the child's
 identity bit with process-restrict-cap before the child runs. The
 child then tries to read its own label and its parent's, and reports
 both over a kernel channel. Both reads must be refused.

 This is the gate, and until the readers were gated it did not exist.
 identity-whoami and identity-get-proc did range checks only, so
 restricting bit 15 changed nothing about them: this test applied a
 capability restriction and then asserted the restriction had no
 effect. It now asserts the denial. The positive direction — an
 unrestricted child inherits the capability and reads successfully —
 is held by identity-inherit and identity-get-proc-test.

 Channels and spawning are Concurrent, identity-set and the reads are
 Identity, process-restrict-cap is Capability; the opening declares
 all three plus Console.

Section: Body
  send-second : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Concurrent] Integer
  send-second (ch) (b) (first) = chan-kern-send ch b

  child-body : Integer, Integer -> [Concurrent, Identity] Integer
  child-body (ch) (x) =
    send-second ch (identity-get-proc 0 0) (chan-kern-send ch (identity-whoami 0))

  recv-after-wait : Integer, Integer -> [Concurrent] Integer
  recv-after-wait (ch) (child) =
    let wt = process-wait child
    in chan-kern-recv ch

  gate-verdict : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  gate-verdict (child-own) (child-saw-parent) (restrict-id) (parent-id) =
    if restrict-id /= 0 then "FAIL: restrict failed"
    else if parent-id == 0 then "FAIL: parent identity not set"
    else if child-own /= (0 - 1) then "FAIL: restricted child read its own identity"
    else if child-saw-parent /= (0 - 1) then "FAIL: restricted child read the parent identity"
    else "PASS"

  opening : [Console, Identity, Concurrent, Capability] Nothing = act
    ch <- chan-kern-create 4
    s <- identity-set 0 hardware-random
    child <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body ch x)
    restrict-id <- process-restrict-cap child 15
    child-own <- recv-after-wait ch child
    child-saw-parent <- chan-kern-recv ch
    print-line-uni (gate-verdict child-own child-saw-parent restrict-id (identity-whoami 0))
  end
